<html><meta charset="utf-8"><style>body{font:17px Georgia;max-width:1100px;margin:30px auto;line-height:1.5}td,th{padding:8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ccc}img{max-width:100%}</style><h1>Task A: CUDA recovery report</h1><p><b>All six validation references passed. This validates initial Task A recovery only; continual-learning benefit has not been evaluated.</b></p><p>Original controller: 3/6 trials failed physically. No continual-learning comparison has run in this recovery stage.</p><table><tr><th>Reference</th><th>Completed</th><th>Motion RMSE (deg)</th><th>Partial RMSE (deg)</th><th>Peak motion error (deg)</th><th>Passed</th></tr><tr><td>A_90_A_e50_validation_00</td><td>True</td><td>0.024160346902077596</td><td>None</td><td>0.06907000506957667</td><td>True</td></tr><tr><td>A_90_A_e60_validation_00</td><td>True</td><td>0.024397236730426024</td><td>None</td><td>0.06419110342251957</td><td>True</td></tr><tr><td>A_90_A_e70_validation_00</td><td>True</td><td>0.02070101742379272</td><td>None</td><td>0.0591723527759503</td><td>True</td></tr><tr><td>A_90_B_e50_validation_00</td><td>True</td><td>0.0155076991357402</td><td>None</td><td>0.04248727646877108</td><td>True</td></tr><tr><td>A_90_B_e60_validation_00</td><td>True</td><td>0.018215642776041128</td><td>None</td><td>0.03933156426680999</td><td>True</td></tr><tr><td>A_90_B_e80_validation_00</td><td>True</td><td>0.022251325161983204</td><td>None</td><td>0.048971086243411184</td><td>True</td></tr></table><h2>Method and limitations</h2><p>Same 28-64-64-1 tanh direct-force NN (6081 parameters), initialized from your existing 600-epoch CUDA checkpoint. No PID is added at deployment. All A_90 training trajectory/query rows are reused; held-out tests are not decoded. Training weights: first 0.25 s 25; remaining first 1 s 8; other trajectory rows 1; teacher probes 6. Loss: weighted normalized-force MSE plus 0.1 times a finite-difference corrective-response penalty on up to 128 training examples per batch. The penalty encourages (but does not guarantee) increasing flexor force when actual angle or velocity decreases at fixed reference; minimum encoded directional slope 0.02, step 0.05. Adam lr=0.0001, batch 2048, maximum 200 epochs. Validation rollouts at epochs 50,100,200 (clipped to the requested budget); stop at the first all-reference pass. Otherwise report the candidate with fewest failed/inaccurate references, then lowest worst complete/partial RMSE. Validation-guided repair is development; no held-out test claims. OpenSim physics uses CPU workers; NN optimization uses CUDA only.</p><h2>Data and training</h2><pre>{
